n prison  occupying himself with a bouncy ball in  the same vein when an adult hears a  rousing track  people who died play over the opening  credits perhaps they'll realize that  this is a song by poet and punk rocker  jim carroll  and that all of those people in the song  really did die in the ways being  described  for greater detail about many of those  unfortunate acquaintances of carol  born to a working class irish family in  new york's lower east side perhaps the  adults may have read carol's  autobiographical book the basketball  diaries  or at least seen the 1995 leonardo  dicaprio film  of the same name that starred leo as  carole  [Music]  from louis prima to pixies the suicide  squad soundtrack is as catchy as it is a  gateway to multiple generations  and the multiple subtext these musicians  bring to mind  james gunn is a master using pop music  to give added dimension to a scene  and he selects most of his soundtracks  while he writes his films  creating scenes around the feelings and  associations that a song carries with it  to a younger person maybe this song just  sounds cool so this is your chance to  talk about  music old and new and the more they know  about these musicians the more they'll  appreciate the film next time they watch  it  a couple decades back an urban legend  spread from coast to coast about a  certain movie star who will not be named  here you have search engines  who supposedly had a thing for gerbils  it's not true but it evidently captured  the imagination of an entire generation  many of whom probably still think  there's something to it flash forward to  today and you have an antagonistic  dynamic in the suicide squad between  ratcatcher 2 and the thinker  in one contentious moment she asked him  do you want a dozen angry rodents  crawling up your ass  to which he responds my answer may not  be what you expect  the exchange seems more likely to get a  laugh from an adult than a teen  possibly because that adult remembers  